                <pb facs="0103" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 33.</note>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Mr. E. B.
                        Washburne.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 164.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 13, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: A dispatch, dated the 22d ultimo, has been
                    received from Mr. Bancroft, in which he mentions the satisfaction with which
                    your course in regard to the subjects of North Germany is viewed by that
                    government. He incloses a copy of a note upon the subject received by him from
                    the Secretary of State, a translation of which, he informs me, he has sent to to
                    you. I am pleased to assure you that your course has given equal satisfaction to
                    this Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
